<spell-notebook "menu theming">
	<header level="1">
		Menu
		<header>A menu displays grouped navigation actions.</>
	</>
	<menu-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-menu-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a header, `:root`), or on
			the menu's box through `::part(menu)`. The items read them from the menu, so set them there or above, not on an
			item. Style an item's box with `ui-item::part(item)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-menu {
			  --ui-menu-radius: 0;
			  --ui-menu-item-padding: 0.75em 1.5em;
			}
			/* one menu's current item */
			ui-menu.site-nav {
			  --ui-menu-active-background: var(--ui-primary);
			  --ui-menu-active-color: white;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				A variation swaps its own values in over the generic tokens, so a theme's `:root` look for the plain menu
				never leaks into a secondary or text one. What `direction="vertical"` and the `secondary`, `text` and `segmented` looks swap has a
				token of its own, `--ui-menu-<variation>-*`: `--ui-menu-secondary-item-padding`,
				`--ui-menu-vertical-icon-float`, `--ui-menu-text-item-color`, `--ui-menu-segmented-active-shadow` ... (all
				in the table below). `--ui-menu-active-first-radius` / `--ui-menu-active-last-radius` default to the
				menu's own corners on that side, by layout. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-menu" playground>
				<ui-menu items="3" aria-label="Menu demo">
					<ui-item link="#editorials" selected>Editorials</>
					<ui-item link="#reviews">Reviews</>
					<ui-item link="#events">Upcoming Events</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
